{% endfor %}
Choose the main affected product based on the actual diff and surrounding code, not a keyword in PR text. Product-specific components, colors and styling go to the product owner, not the design-system owner. Choose `design-system` only for shared, non-product-specific work. For a cross-area PR choose the main affected area; request only one design review. Use `unmapped` only if none of these areas applies; that retains team rotation.
{% endif %}
Reuse the existing review request: do not create another card, pass `inline_summary`, name a reviewer yourself, replace the engineering reviewer, or use `assign_human_reviewer` for this review.
Open SWE chooses the mapped owner (otherwise rotates an available team member), requests them on GitHub, and sends one concise Slack ping in the review thread, with a DM only as a delivery fallback.
This is supplementary, not a new merge gate; their approval must not substitute engineering review.

If the criteria are not met, do nothing.
Never undraft a PR or request a supplementary review while it is a draft.
Do not post a separate channel message, progress narration, or a completion message for this automatic assessment.
